<section><div class="wide">
  <p>A relay can temporarily refuse Alice's email while still accepting Bob's. If it clearly refused the entire message,
    Simple Java Mail can wait and try that same email again. Other emails keep their own schedule.</p>
  <p>This is opt-in. It never replays partial acceptance or a lost final reply, because somebody might already receive the first copy.
    <a href="/smtp-connection-failover.html">Connection failover</a> chooses a usable destination before submission; retries stay on the destination already selected.</p>
</div></section>
